  "summary": "This study compares three Ti3C2Tx electrodes: the HF-etched starting MXene, LiCl-KCl molten-salt-treated M-Ti3C2Tx, and LiCl-KCl-K2CO3-treated KM-Ti3C2Tx. The molten-salt treatments were conducted at 450 \u00b0C for 12 h, while K2CO3 enabled potassium oxygenated-complex intercalation and substantial replacement of \u2013F by \u2013O terminations. KM-Ti3C2Tx is the headline and best-performing electrode, reporting 340 F g\u22121 at 0.5 A g\u22121 in 1 M H2SO4; the abstract/conclusion additionally report 323.6 F g\u22121 at 1 A g\u22121. No BET surface area, porosity, pore diameter, electrode thickness, areal loading, or volumetric/areal capacitance was reported."
